      "message": "Maybe I\u0027m tired, but I\u0027m deeply confused by what this code is trying to do.\n\n- If there is a VPN with this address, then no exemption, so destroy all sockets with this address ?\n- If there is no VPN with this address, then exempt all networks with this address except the passed netId, so destroy only for this netId ?\n\nIf that understanding is correct I think you can replace this entire function with something like\n\n    if (there is a VPN) {\n      destroy(address, Range.create(min, max), null, nai.nc.getUids(), 0, mask);\n    } else {\n      destroy(address, Range.create(nai.netId, nai.netId), null, null, 0, mask);\n    }\n\nAm I missing something ?\n\n\nAlso this is happening whenever any agent updates its link properties, so IIUC, as long as there is a VPN with this address, any network losing this address will destroy all sockets with this source address on other networks ? Is this what we want to do ?",
